Count number of Nice subarrays
Given an array nums and an integer k. An array is called nice if and only if it contains k odd numbers. Find the number of nice subarrays in the given array nums.

A subarray is continuous part of the array.


Example 1
Input : nums = [1, 1, 2, 1, 1] , k = 3
Output : 2
Explanation : The subarrays with three odd numbers are
[1, 1, 2, 1]
[1, 2, 1, 1]

Example 2
Input : nums = [4, 8, 2] , k = 1
Output : 0
Explanation : The array does not contain any odd number.

Better Approach: Binary Subarray Count

Solution:
public class Main{
    public static void main(String args[]){
        int arr[]={1, 1, 2, 1, 1};int goal=3;
        System.out.println(Binary_Sub_Count(arr, goal)- Binary_Sub_Count(arr,goal-1));
    }
    public static int Binary_Sub_Count(int arr[], int k){
      int n=arr.length;
      int left_pointer=0;
      int right_pointer=0;
      int sum=0;
      int SubArray_Count=0;

      while(right_pointer<n){
       sum+=(arr[right_pointer] % 2);
       
       //Invalid Condition
       while(sum>k){
        sum-=(arr[left_pointer] % 2);
        left_pointer++;
       }

       //Valid Condition
       SubArray_Count=SubArray_Count+(right_pointer-left_pointer+1);
       right_pointer++;
      }

      return SubArray_Count;
    }
}
